<title>USA: NetLive settles dispute with banker.</title>
<headline>NetLive settles dispute with banker.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>NetLive Communications Inc said Monday that it has settled corporate governance issues with May Davis Group Inc, the company's investment banker and underwriter of its initial public offering in August 1996.</p>
<p>As part of the settlement agreement, NetLive will increase the size of its board of directors to seven and stagger terms of the directors. The two new vacancies will be filled by one designee of May Davis and one designee of netLive's founders.</p>
<p>NetLive said that May Davis is withdrawing its demand for a consent solicitation and both parties have agreed to release each other from claims or lawsuits.</p>
</text>
